# promise: #602
# A Boost's colours tint the page but leave its pictures alone, as Arc's do (Arc 1.174, 20 Nov 2026: Wikipedia's
# photos kept their pixels under a strong tint). The boosted page is grey with a solid orange picture: the grey
# takes Arc's colorize (140/102/167 for hue 0.7, strength 0.6; Boost.tint, measured in Arc 21 Nov 2026) and the
# picture stays 240/120/20. The engine draws the tint (cc::ColorFilter::MakeCraColorize via
# GraphicsContext::SetCraTint); the CSS filter Cra used before turned the grey 150/141/255, engine -7's matrix
# 152/137/196.
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
port 47602
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false}
seed boosts.json [{"id":"7B1E0D2C-6A43-4F0A-9E3B-60202D000602","host":"127.0.0.1","name":"Tint","enabled":true,"hue":0.7,"strength":0.6,"invert":false,"contrast":50,"brightness":50,"saturation":50,"textScale":1,"textCase":"none","zapped":[],"css":"","js":""}]
cra://open?url=${ORIGIN}/boost-tint.html
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
# Three samples 2 s apart: once, right after the full suite at load, the first read was off by up to 4. Neither the
# old CSS filter's blue 255 nor the matrix's 152/137/196 matches.
wait 2
cra://debug?pagePixel=page&x=40&y=400
wait 2
cra://debug?pagePixel=page&x=40&y=400
wait 2
cra://debug?pagePixel=page&x=40&y=400
expect-log Cra page pixel page: 1(3[7-9]|4[0-3])/(99|10[0-5])/(16[4-9]|170)$
cra://debug?pagePixel=picture&x=400&y=140
expect-log Cra page pixel picture: 2(3[8-9]|4[0-2])/1(1[8-9]|2[0-2])/(1[8-9]|2[0-2])$
# Red and blue have one lightness, so Arc's colorize makes both 148/41/227; a colour matrix keeps them apart.
cra://debug?pagePixel=red&x=350&y=350
expect-log Cra page pixel red: 14[5-9]/(3[8-9]|4[0-4])/2(2[4-9]|30)$
cra://debug?pagePixel=blue&x=500&y=350
expect-log Cra page pixel blue: 14[5-9]/(3[8-9]|4[0-4])/2(2[4-9]|30)$
